---
title: Winter Vegetable Chilli with Avocado Salsa
author: Shirley Simmonds
servings: 10
---

Heat @olive oil{3%tbsp} in a large #pan{}. Cook @large onion{2}(sliced) and @garlic{3%clove}(crushed) for about ~{3%minutes}, or until soft.

Add @large potato{4}(peeled and cubed), @head of celery{1}(thickly sliced), @large carrot{6}(peeled and sliced), @parsnip{4}(peeled and cubed), and @chestnut mushroom{450%g}(halved) and turn to coat in oil. Stir in @ground cumin{3%tsp}, @ground coriander{3%tsp}, and @chilli powder{5%tsp} and cook for ~{2%minutes}.

Add @chopped tomatoes{2%tin}, @red wine{150%ml}, and @tomato puree{5%tbsp}. Cover the pan and simmer for ~{40%minutes} until vegetables are tender.

Add @red kidney beans{3%tin}(drained), @apricot jam{2%tbsp}, and juice of @lemon{1} and season to taste with @salt{} and @ground black pepper{}. The chilli should be hot enough without adding pepper. Simmer uncovered for a further ~{20%minutes}.

For the salsa: roughly chop @avocado{3}(ripe)(peeled and stoned), combine with @Greek yoghurt{250%g}, @lemon juice{2%tbsp}, @red onion{1}(finely chopped), and @fresh coriander{4%tbsp}(chopped) and season to taste.

Spoon the chilli into individual bowls, top with the salsa, and serve with plenty of spicy warmed tortilla chips, green salad, and fresh brown bread.
